# Files excluded from the Railway build context.
#
# The API needs very little: backend/app, backend/models, backend/vendor,
# backend/run.py, requirements.txt and railway.json. Everything below was
# being uploaded and baked into the image for no reason.

# ~50MB: raw spreadsheets, derived CSVs, and a second copy of every model
# artifact. The serving process never reads any of it -- models load from
# backend/models/ (put there by scripts/sync_models.py), and the backtest is
# precomputed into the database by a script run locally, never at request
# time. RESEARCH_MODELS_DIR in app/config.py is a path constant used only by
# that sync script, which does not run on this host.
research/

# Config for the other half of the split deployment (the Vercel CDN).
vercel.json
.vercelignore

# Local-only artifacts. backend/data/ holds backtest_predictions.csv, an audit
# artifact written by run_backtest.py; the API reads backtest results from the
# database, never from this file.
backend/data/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.ipynb
.claude/

# NOTE: frontend/ is deliberately NOT excluded. It is only ~1.8MB, and keeping
# it means the Railway host also serves the dashboard at / as a fallback if the
# Vercel CDN is unreachable during a demo. Add `frontend/` here to make this
# service API-only -- which is what the StaticFiles mount in app/main.py
# already expects in production ("this directory is usually absent").
